    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a2-a32">

                <pb facs="0379" n="369" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg369"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 32 in No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head>The Secretary to the Admiralty to Rear-Admiral Sir B. Walker.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Admiralty,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 1, 1861.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I am commanded by my lords commissioners of
                    the admiralty to send you herewith, for your information and guidance, a copy of
                    a letter from her Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs
                    dated this day, informing my lords that, with a view more effectually to carry
                    out the principle of neutrality, her Majesty’s government proposes to interdict
                    the armed ships of both contending parties in North America from carrying prizes
                    made by them into the ports, harbors, roadsteads, or waters of the United
                    Kingdom, or of any other of her Majesty’s colonies or possessions abroad.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. G. ROMAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
